#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""NewsLens NL-17 M1 entity-backfill proposal launcher.

Thin on purpose (the scripts/doctor + scripts/follow-altitude pattern):
bootstraps sys.path so the runner works from a fresh checkout, then delegates to
src/newslens/backfill.py. All logic lives there and is offline-testable.

    scripts/nl17-backfill                # print the proposal (read-only)
    scripts/nl17-backfill --out DIR      # …and write DIR/proposal.json
    scripts/nl17-backfill --apply        # apply the M1-BLESSED items ONLY

BY DEFAULT: READ-ONLY, $0, ZERO MODEL CALLS. Classification re-reads answers the
resolver already gave and stored (the 0019 disclosure columns); it never
re-resolves, so the same record always produces the same list. Without --apply
the record is opened read-only, so a propose run cannot write to it even by
mistake.

`--apply` (NL-17 M3) writes the M1-BLESSED items and nothing else. DECISIONS
[2026-08-08] "M1 CHECKPOINT RULED" item 4 blessed the LIST, and the bless is
both the authority and the ceiling: an entity item not on
`backfill.BLESSED_ENTITY_ITEMS` is refused BY NAME. It touches
`memory.entity_id` and the entities table only, never the no-entity buckets.
(This header previously read "there is NO --apply … application is M4" — the CoS
resequenced application to M3 with the bless in hand; QA fix loop 1, F-6.)

The proposal is the principal's to read and bless. The no-entity COUNT is the
evidence the product council routed to him for ratifying the case-(a) terminal
reading.
"""

import sys
from pathlib import Path

PROTOTYPE_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(PROTOTYPE_ROOT / "src"))

from newslens.backfill import main  # noqa: E402  (path bootstrap first)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
